   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "c2h",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 772,
   "width": 552,
   "height": 18,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100061,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700427,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "the alternative: a global 'who is connected where' registry",
   "originalText": "the alternative: a global 'who is connected where' registry",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "c2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 798,
   "width": 651,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100062,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700434,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The sender's server looks up the friend list, finds where each friend is connected, and\nsends 40 targeted messages. That requires a global registry consulted on EVERY update -\n333,000 lookups/sec, each returning 40 rows - and rewritten on every connect and\ndisconnect, for 10 million connections that churn constantly.\n\nPublishing to your own channel inverts the problem: instead of the sender finding the\nlisteners, the listeners find the sender, once, at subscribe time.",
   "originalText": "The sender's server looks up the friend list, finds where each friend is connected, and\nsends 40 targeted messages. That requires a global registry consulted on EVERY update -\n333,000 lookups/sec, each returning 40 rows - and rewritten on every connect and\ndisconnect, for 10 million connections that churn constantly.\n\nPublishing to your own channel inverts the problem: instead of the sender finding the\nlisteners, the listeners find the sender, once, at subscribe time.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
