   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "a restart may drop in-flight updates",
   "originalText": "a restart may drop in-flight updates",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bd_1130",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1156,
   "y": 1046,
   "width": 309,
   "height": 30,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100073,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700511,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "and nobody has to reconcile anything\nafterwards, because nothing was promised.",
   "originalText": "and nobody has to reconcile anything\nafterwards, because nothing was promised.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1112,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100074,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700518,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "If a location update were durable-or-bust, every one of 333,000/sec would need an acknowledged, replicated write - a\nWALLET-GRADE durability requirement applied to data that is worthless in 30 seconds. But the next update arrives in 30\nseconds and corrects everything, so: SELF-CORRECTING DATA DOES NOT NEED DURABILITY. Recognising which data has that property\nis what separates this design from an over-engineered one.",
   "originalText": "If a location update were durable-or-bust, every one of 333,000/sec would need an acknowledged, replicated write - a\nWALLET-GRADE durability requirement applied to data that is worthless in 30 seconds. But the next update arrives in 30\nseconds and corrects everything, so: SELF-CORRECTING DATA DOES NOT NEED DURABILITY. Recognising which data has that property\nis what separates this design from an over-engineered one.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
