  {
   "id": "en",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1404,
   "width": 1003,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100085,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700595,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "So the cluster is sized entirely by PUSH THROUGHPUT and the memory is incidental - it is CPU-bound, not memory-bound, which\nis the opposite of most cache-cluster sizing. Two more numbers worth separating: the live location cache is 10M x ~100 bytes\n= about 1 GB, trivial and bounded by the TTL rather than by growth; while location HISTORY is 333,000 rows/sec retained\nforever at ~40 bytes = 1.15 TB/DAY. That is not the live feature - it is an append-only analytics stream with completely\ndifferent requirements, which is why it lives in a different store.",
   "originalText": "So the cluster is sized entirely by PUSH THROUGHPUT and the memory is incidental - it is CPU-bound, not memory-bound, which\nis the opposite of most cache-cluster sizing. Two more numbers worth separating: the live location cache is 10M x ~100 bytes\n= about 1 GB, trivial and bounded by the TTL rather than by growth; while location HISTORY is 333,000 rows/sec retained\nforever at ~40 bytes = 1.15 TB/DAY. That is not the live feature - it is an append-only analytics stream with completely\ndifferent requirements, which is why it lives in a different store.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "en2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1524,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100086,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700602,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And the 30-second refresh is not an arbitrary constant: at a walking speed of 1.4 m/s a person moves ~42 m in 30 s, well\ninside any useful radius - so anything faster multiplies the 13.3M number for no user-visible benefit.",
   "originalText": "And the 30-second refresh is not an arbitrary constant: at a walking speed of 1.4 m/s a person moves ~42 m in 30 s, well\ninside any useful radius - so anything faster multiplies the 13.3M number for no user-visible benefit.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
